Subject: Prototype shapes with a deleted property are hashed at cache sites

What this does
  regvm_shape_hashify leaves a shape with a deleted property unhashed (0606) only for a receiver that is an ordinary object. The holder, middle and receiver shapes of prototype objects are hashed as before 0606.

Why we need it
  0606 targeted ordinary objects, where every delete makes a fresh copy of the shape. A prototype that lost a property keeps one long-lived shape, and leaving it unhashed sent every site reading through it to the uncached path: the kit kernel protochange (`delete Q.prototype.extra`, then calls through instances) went from 280.2 to 411.2 M instructions compiled. Now 275.9 M (94.5 M cycles, was 131.3). dispatch_delete_shape keeps 0606's gain (303 M cycles compiled, 395 M interpreted).

Soundness
  Hashing a prototype's shape is what the code did before 0606, so these sites work as they did then; only ordinary objects' deleted-property copies stay unhashed, which their sites already handle (need_mega).

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 348ba2b..5b8486f 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -29503,4 +29503,6 @@ static void regvm_pic_install(JSRuntime *rt, JSRegPIC *e, JSShape **pholder,
- * only maintained while `is_hashed`. A shape with a deleted property is left
- * as it is: every delete makes its own copy, which no transition reaches, so
- * hashing them puts one more equal shape in the same bucket per object and
- * each free walks the chain. Its sites take the uncached path.
+ * only maintained while `is_hashed`. An ordinary object's shape with a deleted
+ * property (`copy`) is left as it is: every delete makes the object its own
+ * copy, which no transition reaches, so hashing them puts one more equal shape
+ * in the same bucket per object and each free walks the chain. Its sites take
+ * the uncached path. A prototype's shape is one long-lived shape however many
+ * objects read through it, so it is hashed even with a deleted property.
@@ -29508 +29510 @@ static void regvm_pic_install(JSRuntime *rt, JSRegPIC *e, JSShape **pholder,
-static void regvm_shape_hashify(JSRuntime *rt, JSShape *sh)
+static void regvm_shape_hashify(JSRuntime *rt, JSShape *sh, bool copy)
@@ -29512 +29514 @@ static void regvm_shape_hashify(JSRuntime *rt, JSShape *sh)
-    if (sh->is_hashed || sh->deleted_prop_count != 0)
+    if (sh->is_hashed || (copy && sh->deleted_prop_count != 0))
@@ -29597 +29599 @@ static void regvm_pic_fill(JSContext *ctx, JSFunctionBytecode *b,
-        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, rsh);
+        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, rsh, !p->is_prototype);
@@ -29599 +29601 @@ static void regvm_pic_fill(JSContext *ctx, JSFunctionBytecode *b,
-            regvm_shape_hashify(rt, hsh);
+            regvm_shape_hashify(rt, hsh, false);
@@ -29601,3 +29603,3 @@ static void regvm_pic_fill(JSContext *ctx, JSFunctionBytecode *b,
-        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, rsh);
-        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, mid);
-        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, holder->shape);
+        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, rsh, !p->is_prototype);
+        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, mid, false);
+        regvm_shape_hashify(rt, holder->shape, false);
@@ -70554 +70556 @@ QJS_AOT_STUB JSValue qjs_aot_gated_call(JSContext *ctx, JSObject *co, JSValue th
-static void regvm_shape_hashify(JSRuntime *rt, JSShape *sh);
+static void regvm_shape_hashify(JSRuntime *rt, JSShape *sh, bool copy);
